## Description

The swagger spec for `POST /characters/{character_id}/contacts/` and `PUT /characters/{character_id}/contacts/` documents `standing`, `contact_ids`, `label_ids`, and `watched` as request body parameters. However, ESI rejects the request body and only reads these values from query parameters.

## Reproduction

Using the spec as documented (sending parameters in the request body):

```typescript
// This fails — ESI ignores the body
fetch('https://esi.evetech.net/latest/characters/{id}/contacts/', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ...' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ standing: 5, contact_ids: [90404873] })
});
// Returns 500 or ignores the contact_ids
```

Using query parameters instead (not documented in spec):

```typescript
// This works — ESI reads from query params
fetch('https://esi.evetech.net/latest/characters/{id}/contacts/?standing=5&contact_ids=90404873', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer ...' }
});
// Successfully adds the contact
```

## Affected Endpoints

- `POST /characters/{character_id}/contacts/` — `standing` and `contact_ids` must be query params
- `PUT /characters/{character_id}/contacts/` — same parameters, same issue
- `DELETE /characters/{character_id}/contacts/` — `contact_ids` must be comma-separated query param (previously reported in #342, which was closed as resolved via v2, but the `/latest/` route still has this behavior)

## Impact

Any client generated from the swagger spec (e.g., via `openapi-typescript` or `openapi-generator`) will produce non-functional contacts endpoints. The generated code sends parameters in the request body as the spec documents, but ESI silently ignores the body.

## Workaround

In [ESI.ts](https://github.com/lgriffin/ESI.ts) we work around this by routing these parameters through query string construction instead of the request body, despite what the spec says. See: `src/core/endpoints/contactEndpoints.ts` and `src/clients/ContactsClient.ts`.

## Related

- #342 — covered the DELETE case specifically (closed)
- #184, #199 — other contacts spec inconsistencies (closed)
EOF
