## Description

The swagger spec for all 4 UI window endpoints documents parameters as request body, but ESI only reads them from query parameters. Sending the parameters in the request body results in ESI ignoring them.

## Affected Endpoints

| Endpoint | Parameters affected |
|---|---|
| `POST /ui/autopilot/waypoint/` | `destination_id`, `add_to_beginning`, `clear_other_waypoints` |
| `POST /ui/openwindow/contract/` | `contract_id` |
| `POST /ui/openwindow/information/` | `target_id` |
| `POST /ui/openwindow/marketdetails/` | `type_id` |

`POST /ui/openwindow/newmail/` is the exception — it correctly uses the request body for the mail composition data.

## Reproduction

```typescript
// This fails — ESI ignores the body
await fetch('https://esi.evetech.net/latest/ui/autopilot/waypoint/', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ...' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    destination_id: 30002510,
    add_to_beginning: false,
    clear_other_waypoints: true,
  }),
});
// Returns 204 but does not set the waypoint

// This works — parameters as query string
await fetch(
  'https://esi.evetech.net/latest/ui/autopilot/waypoint/' +
    '?destination_id=30002510&add_to_beginning=false&clear_other_waypoints=true',
  {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer ...' },
  },
);
// Returns 204 and sets the waypoint in the EVE client
```

Same pattern applies to the contract, information, and market detail window endpoints.

## Impact

Any client generated from the swagger spec will produce non-functional UI endpoints. The generated code sends parameters in the request body, but ESI ignores the body and reads only from query parameters.

## Workaround

In [ESI.ts](https://github.com/lgriffin/ESI.ts) we work around this by routing these parameters through query string construction. See: `src/core/endpoints/uiEndpoints.ts` and `src/clients/UiClient.ts`.
EOF
)"","description":"Open ESI issue for UI body-vs-query"}

Bash {"command":"gh issue create --repo esi/esi-issues \
  --title "Fleet wing/squad name 10-character limit not documented in swagger spec" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Description

The `PUT /fleets/{fleet_id}/wings/{wing_id}/` and `PUT /fleets/{fleet_id}/squads/{squad_id}/` endpoints enforce a maximum name length of 10 characters, but this constraint is not documented in the swagger spec. The `naming` field in the request body schema has no `maxLength` property.

## Reproduction

```typescript
await fetch('https://esi.evetech.net/latest/fleets/{fleet_id}/wings/{wing_id}/', {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Authorization': 'Bearer ...',
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Compat Test' }), // 11 characters
});
// Returns 400: "'Compat Test' exceeds the maximum length of 10"
```

Shortening to 10 characters or fewer succeeds:

```typescript
body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Alpha' }), // 5 characters
// Returns 204 — wing renamed successfully
```

## Expected

The swagger spec should include `maxLength: 10` on the `naming` field for both endpoints, so that generated clients and API documentation reflect the actual constraint.

## Affected Endpoints

- `PUT /fleets/{fleet_id}/wings/{wing_id}/` — `naming.name` field
- `PUT /fleets/{fleet_id}/squads/{squad_id}/` — `naming.name` field

## Workaround

In [ESI.ts](https://github.com/lgriffin/ESI.ts) we validate the name length client-side before sending the request:

```typescript
renameFleetSquad(fleetId: number, squadId: number, name: string): Promise<void> {
  if (name.length > 10) {
    return Promise.reject(
      new Error(`Fleet squad name "${name}" exceeds ESI maximum of 10 characters`)
    );
  }
  return this.api.renameFleetSquad(fleetId, squadId, name);
}
```

See: `src/clients/FleetClient.ts`.
EOF
